\section{Unified Action Principle}

The entire framework is derived from the \textbf{SATO/Blockwave Transitional Lagrangian (SATO-BLOCK-INT)}, which integrates all fields and constraints into a single action $$:
\[
\mathbf{S\_{\text{SATO/Blockwave}} = \int d^4x \sqrt{-g} \left[ \mathcal{L}_{\text{Grav}} + \mathcal{L}_{\theta} + \mathcal{L}_{u} + \mathcal{L}_{\text{Gauge}} + \mathcal{L}_{\text{int}} \right] + S_{\text{Top}}}
\]
where $\mathcal{L}$ are continuous Lagrangian densities and $S_{\text{Top}}$ is the Discrete Topological Constraint Action $$. The fundamental fields are the Unit Time-Flow Vector ($\mathbf{u^\mu}$), the Misalignment Angle ($\mathbf{\theta_4}$), the Scalar Phase ($\mathbf{\psi}$), and the Discrete Twist Field ($\mathbf{\tau}$) $$.

