    The fermionic field ($\psi^a$) dynamics are rigorously derived to match the covariant Dirac equation coupled to the emergent strong gauge field ($A^A_\mu$):
    \[
    \boxed{
    (i \gamma^\mu D_\mu - m) \psi^a = 0,
    }
    \]
    with the covariant derivative $D_\mu = \partial_\mu + i g_s A^A_\mu T^A$.

    \item \textbf{Gravitational Wave Modification (EOM)}:
    The EOM for high-frequency gravitational wave propagation is derived from the linearized strain perturbations ($\delta u^\mu(x)$). The model predicts deviations relative to General Relativity due to strain-induced corrections from the foliation field $\mathbf{u^\mu(x)}$.
